hadiths[56]{hadithnumber,text}:
"54","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that (one day) while the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting in a gathering and speaking to the people, a Bedouin came to him and asked, ""When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) be established?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not reply to him and continued speaking. Upon this, some people said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had heard what he said but disliked it and therefore did not answer, while others said that he had not heard it. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) finished his speech, he said, ""Where is the questioner?"" I think these were the words after that: ""The one who asked about the Hour?"" The questioner said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Here I am."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""When trust is lost, then await the Hour (i.e., the Day of Judgment is near)."" He asked, ""How will trust be lost?"" He replied, ""When matters are entrusted to those who are not qualified, then await the Hour."""
"55","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` during a journey which we undertook in the company of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), the Prophet (peace be upon him) lagged behind us. Then he (peace be upon him) met us while we had delayed the prayer and were performing ablution, so (due to haste) we began to pass water over our feet (because washing them takes time). Upon this, the Prophet (peace be upon him) raised his voice and said two or three times: ""Woe to the heels from the fire (of punishment)"" (i.e., if left dry)."
"56","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Among the trees, there is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it resembles a Muslim. So tell me, which tree is that?"" The people started thinking of the wild trees. Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: It came to my mind that it is the date-palm tree, but I felt shy to say it. Eventually, the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) submitted: O Messenger of Allah! Please tell us which tree it is. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is the date-palm tree."""
"57","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` once we were sitting in the mosque with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) when a man came riding a camel. He brought his camel into the mosque, made it sit down, and tied its legs. Then he asked the companions (may Allah be pleased with them), ""Who among you is Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" At that time, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting among the companions (may Allah be pleased with them), reclining on a cushion. So we said, ""This fair-complexioned man who is reclining on the cushion (he is Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him)."" Then that man said to you, ""O son of Abdul Muttalib!"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""(Speak,) I am listening."" He said, ""I am going to ask you something and I will be a bit harsh in questioning, so do not find it unpleasant in your heart."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Ask whatever comes to your mind."" He said, ""I ask you by your Lord and the Lord of those before you (tell me the truth), has Allah sent you to all mankind (as a Prophet)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""By Allah! Yes (indeed, I have been sent as a Prophet)."" Then he said, ""I ask you by Allah (tell me the truth), has Allah commanded you to establish five prayers in the day and night?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""By Allah! Yes."" Then he said, ""I ask you by Allah (tell me the truth), has Allah commanded you to fast in this month (i.e., Ramadan)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""By Allah! Yes."" Then he said, ""I ask you by Allah (tell me the truth), has Allah commanded you to take this charity from our wealthy and distribute it among our needy?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""By Allah! Yes."" After that, the man said, ""I have believed in this (Shariah) which you (peace and blessings be upon him) have brought, and I am the representative sent by those of my people who are behind me, and I am Dhamam bin Tha’labah, belonging to the tribe of Banu Sa’d bin Bakr."""
"58","‘Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says:’ The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a letter by the hand of a person and instructed him to deliver this letter to the ruler of Bahrain. (So he delivered it.) And the ruler of Bahrain forwarded it to Kisra (the king of Persia). Then when (Kisra) read it, (out of his wretchedness) he tore it up. (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both,) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard this, he invoked a curse upon those people, saying: “They (too) shall be torn to pieces in the same way.”"
"59","‘Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to write or wrote a letter (to the king of Rome or Persia), it was said to him that those people do not read a letter without a seal (i.e., they do not give it importance). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a silver ring made, on which “Muhammad Rasul Allah” was engraved. (Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: It feels as if) I am (even now) looking at the whiteness of it in the blessed hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"60","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Waqid Al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him) that (one day) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque and people were sitting with him (to benefit from him), three persons came. Two of them came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and one went away. (Abu Waqid, may Allah be pleased with him, says) that both of them stood for a while near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then one of them saw a space in the circle and sat there, and the other sat at the back (where the gathering ended), and the third went away. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished (his sermon), he addressed the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) and said: Shall I not tell you about the condition of these three men? One of them turned to Allah, so Allah gave him a place, the second felt shy, so Allah (also) was shy with him, and the third turned away, so Allah (also) turned away from him."
"61","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on his camel and a man was holding its rein. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) and said: ""What day is this?"" We remained silent until we thought that perhaps the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give it a name other than its (real) name. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is it not the Day of Sacrifice?"" We replied, ""Yes."" Then he asked: ""What month is this?"" Again, we remained silent until we thought that perhaps the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would call it by another name. Then he said: ""Is it not Dhul-Hijjah?"" We replied, ""Yes."" (After this) the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your blood, your wealth, and your honor are as sacred among you as the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this city of yours. Let those who are present convey this message to those who are absent, for perhaps the one who hears it may convey it to someone who will remember it better than the one who heard it."""
"62","`Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose the appropriate time and occasion to advise us, and out of concern that we might become weary (he would not deliver admonition every day)."
"63","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Make things easy (in religion) and do not make them difficult, and give glad tidings and do not make people averse (by scaring them excessively)."
"64","Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah intends good for someone, He grants him understanding of the religion. And (the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) I am only a distributor, and it is Allah Who gives. And remember, this Ummah will always remain established on Allah’s command (the religion), so whoever opposes them will not be able to harm them until the Day of Resurrection arrives."
"65","´Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` we were with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) when a date palm stalk was brought to him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Among the trees, there is a tree... (and he narrated the entire hadith). (See the Book: The Statement of Knowledge... Chapter: The Imam asking questions to his companions to test their knowledge...) And in this narration (Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both) added that I was the youngest, so I remained silent."
"66","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Envy (jealousy) is not permissible except in two (types of) people: (1) The person whom Allah has given wealth and granted him the ability and determination to spend it in the (right) way; (2) The person whom Allah has granted knowledge and wisdom, and he judges (and acts) according to it and teaches it to others."
"67","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once embraced me to his chest and said: ""O Allah! Grant him knowledge of Your Book."""
"68","Narrated Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: I once rode a donkey and at that time I was close to puberty, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was offering prayer at Mina without any wall (sutrah) in front of him. I passed in front of part of the row and let the donkey loose so that it could graze, and I joined the row. No one stopped me from doing this."
"69","Narrated by Sayyiduna Mahmud bin Rabi' (may Allah be pleased with him): I remember a spurt of water from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), which he took from a bucket and threw into my mouth, and I was five years old at that time."
"70","`Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: The example of the guidance and knowledge with which Allah has sent me is like that of a heavy rain which falls upon the earth. The land which is clean absorbs the water, then much grass and fodder grows from it. And the land which is hard retains the water. Then Allah benefits people through it; they drink from it, give it to their animals to drink, and irrigate their crops. And some of the rain falls on another part of the land which is a barren plain; it neither retains the water nor grows any vegetation. Thus, this is the example of the person who understands the religion of Allah and benefits from what Allah has sent me with, so he learns it and teaches it. And the example of the person who does not even raise his head towards it and does not accept the guidance with which I have been sent by Allah (is like the barren, waterless land and the plain field)."
"71","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, (these things) are among the signs of the Hour: knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will remain, wine will be drunk in abundance, and adultery will be committed openly."""
"72","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: (Today) I will narrate to you a hadith such that after me (perhaps) no one will narrate it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Among the signs of the Hour is that knowledge will decrease and ignorance will prevail, and adultery will become widespread, and women will increase in number while men will decrease, to the extent that for fifty women there will be only one man to look after (support) them."""
"73","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""While I was sleeping, (in a dream) a bowl of milk was brought to me, so I drank from it until I began to feel that its nourishment was coming out of my fingernails. Then I gave the remainder to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: O Messenger of Allah! What interpretation did you give to it? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Knowledge."""
"74","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Mina for the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage. People would ask him questions about religious matters. Then a man came and said, ""Unknowingly, I shaved my head before sacrificing (the animal)."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(Now) sacrifice (the animal), and there is no harm."" Then another man came and said, ""Unknowingly, I offered the sacrifice before stoning (the Jamarat)."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(Now) perform the stoning, and there is no harm."" (Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that on that day) whatever was asked of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the order of the rites of Hajj, whether it was done earlier or later, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the same: ""Do it now, and there is no harm."""
"75","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""(Soon) knowledge will be taken away, ignorance and tribulations will prevail, and 'harj' will increase greatly."" It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is 'harj'?"" So he (peace be upon him) gestured with his hand sideways and said: ""Like this!"" It seemed that by 'harj' he (peace be upon him) meant killing."
"76","Lady Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I came to Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) and she was praying, so I asked her, ""What is the matter with the people (why are they so anxious)?"" She pointed towards the sky (to show that there was an eclipse of the sun). Then, meanwhile, all the people stood up (for the eclipse prayer), so Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""Subhan Allah."" I asked, ""(Is this eclipse) a sign?"" She nodded her head in affirmation. Then I also stood up (for the prayer), until I fainted and began to pour water over my head. Then (when the prayer was over and the eclipse had passed), the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised and glorified Allah and said: ""That which had not been shown to me before, I saw (at that time) while standing in my place. Even Paradise and Hell. And it was revealed to me that you will be tested in your graves—a trial similar to or close to the trial of the False Messiah (Dajjal)."" (Fatimah, the narrator of the hadith, says: I do not remember which of the two words Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) used.) It will be said, ""What do you know about this man?"" If he is a believer or certain (Fatimah says: I do not remember which of the two words Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) used), he will say, ""He is Muhammad (peace be upon him), the Messenger of Allah. He came to us with miracles and guidance, so we accepted his word and followed him, and he is Muhammad (peace be upon him)."" (He will say this) three times. Then it will be said to him, ""Sleep in peace. Indeed, we have known that you believed in Muhammad (peace be upon him)."" But the hypocrite or the doubter (Fatimah says: I do not remember which of the two words Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) used) will say, ""I do not know (the reality), but I heard people saying something about him, so I said the same."""
"77","Narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him): He married the daughter of Abu Ihab bin Aziz. After that, a woman came and stated that she had suckled Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) and the girl whom Uqbah had married (thus, both are foster brother and sister and their marriage is not valid). Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I do not know that you have suckled me, nor have you ever informed me of this before."" Then Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) rode (from Makkah) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah and asked him (about this issue). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""How (can you now have marital relations with her), when it has been stated (which creates doubt of prohibition)?"" So Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) separated from the woman, and she married another man."
"78","Narrated from Amir al-Mu’minin Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): I and an Ansari neighbor of mine used to live in the locality of Banu Umayyah bin Zaid, which was situated at the higher part of Madinah. We used to take turns to go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day he would go, and one day I would go. On the day I went, I would bring him the news of that day—revelation and other matters—and on the day he went, he would do the same. One day, my Ansari friend came (after attending the Prophet, peace be upon him, on his turn) and knocked at my door very hard and called out my name, “Is he here?” I got scared by his agitated manner and came out to him. He said, “A great event has happened (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, has divorced his wives)!” I went to Hafsa (Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her), and she was weeping. I asked her, “Did the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) divorce you all?” She replied, “I do not know.” Then I went to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and, while standing, I asked, “Did you divorce your wives?” He replied, “No.” At that, I exclaimed in great astonishment, “Allahu Akbar!” (How mistaken the Ansari was!)"
"79","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I may soon not be able to join the prayer (in congregation), because so-and-so leads us in very lengthy prayers.” Abu Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says, “I have never seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more angry in giving advice than he was that day.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O people! You are those who make others dislike (the religion) (see?), whoever leads the people in prayer should lighten it (i.e., make it short in every posture), because among the followers are the sick, the weak, and those who have needs.”"
"80","Narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the ruling regarding a lost (unclaimed) item. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Recognize its binding,"" or he said, ""its container and its pouch (recognize them), then announce it for a year (i.e., search for its real owner). After that (if no owner is found), benefit from it, and if its owner comes (even after a year), then hand it over to him."" Then that man asked, ""What about a lost camel (if found, what should be done)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until both his blessed cheeks turned red, or (the narrator said) his blessed face turned red, and he said: ""What have you to do with that camel? Its water bag and its shoes are with it, it will reach water (and drink), and eat (leaves) from the trees, so leave it until its owner finds it."" Then that man asked, ""What about a lost goat (is it permissible to take it)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(Take it, because) it is for you, or for your brother, or (if it does not come into anyone's hands) then for the wolf."""
"81","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that (on one occasion) some questions were asked to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which were contrary to his temperament. (So he did not give any answer, but) when there was a flood of such questions before him, he became angry and said: ""Ask me whatever you wish."" So a man said, ""Who is my father?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""Your father is Hudhafah."" Then another man stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who is my father?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""Your father is Salim, the slave of Shaybah."" Then when Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw the signs of anger on the blessed face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! We repent to Allah, the Most Great and Exalted (meaning, we will never ask you such questions again)."""
"82","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said something, he would repeat it three times so that (its meaning could be well) understood. When he came to a group of people and greeted them, he would greet them three times."
"83","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three persons for whom there is a double reward: (1) A person who is from the People of the Book, who believed in his own prophet and (then) also believed in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); (2) A slave, when he fulfills the rights of Allah and the rights of his masters; (3) A person who has a slave-girl, teaches her good manners and gives her excellent training, and gives her good and excellent education, then sets her free and marries her, so for him there is a double reward."
"84","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) went out (on the day of Eid from the men's rows towards the women) and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was with him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) thought that (perhaps) the women had not (properly) heard the sermon, so he advised them and instructed them to give charity. So (some) women started giving their earrings and (some) their rings (and some other things), and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) began collecting them in the corner of his garment."
"85","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he (Abu Hurairah) said: O Messenger of Allah! Who will be the most fortunate of people to receive your intercession on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I was sure, O Abu Hurairah, that no one would ask me about this before you, because I have seen your eagerness for (learning) hadith. So (listen!), the most fortunate of people to receive my intercession on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who says 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah) sincerely from his heart or sincerely from his soul."""
"86","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by removing it from the hearts of the servants, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars (through death), until when no scholar remains, people will take ignorant ones as their leaders (muftis and guides), and they will be asked (religious questions) and will give verdicts without knowledge; they will go astray themselves and will lead others astray."""
"87","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The women said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""The men have surpassed us in benefiting from you, so please appoint a day for us (for admonition)."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised them a day. On that day, he met them, advised them, and commanded them with acts of worship suitable for them. Among what he said to them was: ""Any woman among you whose three children die before her (i.e., they die in her lifetime), they will be a shield for her from the Fire (of Hell)."" A woman asked, ""And if (she loses) two (children)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""And two (as well)."" And in the narration of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), it is mentioned: ""Three children who did not reach the age of puberty."""
"88","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that (on one occasion) the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: “(On the Day of Resurrection) whoever is called to account will be punished.” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said (upon hearing this): “Does Allah not say, ‘Soon an easy account will be taken from him’ (Al-Inshiqaq: 8)?” (It is understood from this that after an easy account, punishment is not necessary.) So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “This (account mentioned in this verse) is not actually an account, but only the presentation of deeds. But whoever is questioned in detail in the account will surely be destroyed.”"
"89","Sayyiduna Abu Shurayh (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a statement on the second day of the conquest of Makkah, which my two ears heard and my heart remembered, and when you (peace be upon him) delivered this (sermon), my eyes were looking at you. You praised and glorified Allah, then said: ""Allah has made Makkah (fighting and the like) sacred; people have not made it sacred. So whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, it is not permissible for him to shed blood in Makkah, nor is it permissible to cut down any tree there. Then if anyone argues for the permissibility of these things by the fighting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makkah, then say to him that Allah gave permission to His Messenger, but He did not give you permission, and I too was only given permission for a short period of the day, then today its sanctity has returned to what it was yesterday. So, those who are present should convey this (news) to those who are absent."""
"90","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not ever lie upon me, for whoever lies upon me should make his abode in the Hellfire."""
"91","Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever attributes to me something which I have not said, then he should find his abode in the Fire.”"
"92","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Keep my name, but do not keep my kunyah (my title, which is Abu al-Qasim) during my lifetime. And (be certain that) whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, because Satan cannot assume my form, cannot take my appearance. And whoever deliberately lies about me should find his place in the Fire."""
"93","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah Almighty prevented the Elephant (the army of elephants) or killing from Makkah, and made His Messenger (peace be upon him) and the believers victorious over them. Be aware, fighting in Makkah was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me. Be aware, it was made lawful for me for only a short period during the day; be aware, (now) it is forbidden at this time. Its thorny plants should not be cut, its trees should not be felled, and its fallen things should not be picked up except by one who announces it (i.e., who seeks its original owner and returns it to him). And if anyone’s (relative) is killed, he has the choice of one of two options: either he is given blood money or retribution is taken (the killer is handed over to the heirs of the slain).” Meanwhile, a man from the people of Yemen came and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Write (this sermon) for me.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, “Write it for Abu So-and-so.” Then a man from the Quraysh said, “(O Messenger of Allah!) Except for idhkhir (a type of grass), (please do not prohibit the cutting of idhkhir, as) we use it in our homes and graves.” So the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) said, “(Yes,) except for idhkhir (the prohibition applies to all other things).”"
"94","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the illness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became severe, he said: ""Bring me writing materials so that I may write a document for you after which you will never go astray."" Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the illness has overwhelmed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (his condition is extremely unwell), and since we have the Book of Allah with us, that is sufficient for us. Then the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) differed until there was much commotion, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Get up from me, and what is the matter of causing dispute in my presence?"""
"95","Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that one night the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up from sleep and said, “Glory be to Allah! How many trials have been sent down tonight and how many treasures have been opened! (O people!) Wake up the women sleeping in these rooms (so that they may worship), for there are many who are clothed in this world who will be naked in the Hereafter (due to lack of good deeds).”"
"96","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once led the ‘Isha prayer in the last part of his blessed life. When he had finished the prayer and said salam, he stood up and said: “Remember this night of yours well (see), from tonight until the end of one hundred years, none of the people who are on the earth today will remain.”"
"97","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I spent a night in the house of my maternal aunt, Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah bint al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her that night. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the 'Isha prayer (in the mosque), then came to his house and prayed four rak'ahs, and then lay down and slept. Then he woke up and said: ""Has the little boy slept?"" or he said something similar. Then he stood up (to pray), and I stood (after performing ablution) on his left side, so he made me stand on his right side. Then he prayed five rak'ahs, after which he prayed two rak'ahs (the Sunnah of Fajr), then lay down until I heard the sound of his snoring. Then he went out for the (Fajr) prayer (to the mosque)."
"98","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say that` people say that Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) has memorized and narrated many hadiths, and if these two verses were not in the Book of Allah, I would not narrate even a single hadith. Then he would recite: ""Indeed, those who conceal the clear proofs and guidance We have sent down... Most Merciful, Most Compassionate."" (Al-Baqarah: 159, 160) Surely, our Muhajir brothers were occupied with buying and selling in the markets, and our Ansari brothers were busy with their wealth and work, and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) would stay with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to fill his stomach, and he would be present at times when others were not present, and he would remember things that others would not remember."
"99","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I hear many hadiths from you but I forget them."" So he said, ""Spread your cloak."" So I spread my cloak, and he scooped with both his hands (and made a symbolic gesture as if pouring something into the cloak), then said, ""Wrap it around yourself."" So I wrapped it around myself, and after that I never forgot anything."
"100","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I memorized two vessels (of knowledge, two types of knowledge) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for one of them, I have made it public; but if I were to disclose the other, my neck would be cut."
"101","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him during the Farewell Pilgrimage: ""Make the people quiet."" (When the people became silent,) then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(O people!) Do not become disbelievers after me, that you start killing each other."""
"102","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka’b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Musa (peace be upon him) once stood to deliver a sermon among the Children of Israel. He was asked, ‘Who is the most knowledgeable among the people?’ He replied, ‘I am the most knowledgeable.’ So Allah reproached him for not attributing knowledge to Allah. Then Allah revealed to him that among My servants there is a servant at the junction of the two seas who is more knowledgeable than you. Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘O my Lord! How can I meet him?’ He was told, ‘Put a fish in a basket (and set out towards the junction of the two seas). When you lose the fish (at a certain place), know that the servant is there.’ So Musa (peace be upon him) set out, taking with him his servant Yusha’ bin Nun, and they placed a fish in a basket. When they reached a rock (a stone), they both rested their heads (on the ground) and slept. (At that place) the fish slipped out of the basket and made its way into the sea. Musa (peace be upon him) and his servant were amazed at the fish coming to life. Then they both continued walking for the rest of the night and a day. When morning came, Musa (peace be upon him) said to his servant, ‘Bring us our breakfast (the meal with the fish), for we have suffered much fatigue from this journey.’ Musa (peace be upon him) did not feel any fatigue until he had passed the place he was commanded to stop at. (When his servant looked, the fish was gone.) He said, ‘Did you see (do you remember) when we rested by the rock? I forgot to mention the fish (completely).’ Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘That is the place we were seeking.’ So they both retraced their steps, following their footprints, until they reached the rock. (What did they see?) A man was sitting, wrapped in a cloth (or he said, he had wrapped a cloth around himself). Musa (peace be upon him) greeted him with salam. Khidr (peace be upon him) said, ‘Where is salam in your land from?’ He replied, ‘I am not from here, I am Musa (peace be upon him).’ Khidr (peace be upon him) said, ‘Musa of the Children of Israel?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘May I follow you so that you may teach me some of the guidance you have been taught?’ He said, ‘You will not be able to have patience with me. O Musa! I have knowledge from Allah which He has especially given to me, which you do not know, and you have knowledge which Allah has taught you, which I do not know.’ Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘If Allah wills, you will find me patient, and I will not disobey you in any matter.’ (So Khidr (peace be upon him) agreed.) Then they both walked along the riverbank, and they had no boat. A boat passed by them, and they asked its people to take them on board. Khidr (peace be upon him) was recognized, and the boat people took them on board without fare. Then a bird came and sat on the edge of the boat and dipped its beak once or twice into the river. Khidr (peace be upon him) said, ‘O Musa! My knowledge and your knowledge, compared to Allah’s knowledge, is only as much as this bird’s beak took from the sea.’ Then Khidr (peace be upon him) went to one of the planks of the boat and pulled it out. Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘These people took us on board without fare, and you have damaged their boat so that its passengers may drown!’ Khidr (peace be upon him) said, ‘Did I not tell you that you would not be able to have patience with me?’ Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘I forgot, so do not hold me accountable, and do not be hard on me in my matter.’ The Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) said that the first time, Musa (peace be upon him) made this objection out of forgetfulness. Then they both (disembarked from the boat and) walked on until they met a boy who was playing with other boys. Khidr (peace be upon him) seized his head from above and killed him with his hand. Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘You have killed an innocent soul without reason!’ Khidr (peace be upon him) said, ‘Did I not tell you that you would not be able to have patience with me?’ Ibn ‘Uyaynah (the narrator of the hadith) said that this time the rebuke was more emphatic than the previous one. Then they both walked on until they came to a town and asked its people for food, but they refused to host them. There they found a wall about to collapse, so Khidr (peace be upon him) supported it with his hand and repaired it. (Then) Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘If you wished, you could have taken a wage for it.’ Khidr (peace be upon him) said, ‘(Now) this is the parting between me and you.’ The Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) said (after narrating this much): ‘May Allah have mercy on Musa (peace be upon him). We wished that Musa (peace be upon him) had been patient, so that more of their story would have been related to us.’"
"103","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by fighting in the way of Allah? For some of us fight out of anger and some fight for (personal or tribal) pride."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his (blessed) head towards him (to pay attention), and (the narrator says) he raised his head because the man was standing. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is exalted (and His word becomes supreme), then he is fighting in the way of Allah."""
"104","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` while I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the ruins of Madinah and he was walking with a palm stick resting on the ground, the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed by some Jews. One of them said to the others, “Ask him (peace be upon him) about the soul.” Some of them said, “Do not ask, lest he says something that you dislike.” Then some said, “We will certainly ask.” So one of them stood up and said, “O Abul Qasim! What is the soul?” The Prophet (peace be upon him) remained silent. (Ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says) I thought to myself that revelation was being sent down upon him. So I stood up. Then, when that state left the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: “And they ask you (O Prophet) about the soul. Say: The soul is by the command of my Lord, and you have been given but little knowledge.”"
"105","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Sayyiduna Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) was riding behind him on the mount, said: “O Mu’adh bin Jabal!” He replied, “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and I am ready.” (Then) the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “O Mu’adh!” He replied, “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and I am ready.” (Then) the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “O Mu’adh!” He replied, “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and I am ready.” This happened three times. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever testifies with a sincere heart that there is no god but Allah and Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, Allah makes the (Hell) fire forbidden for him.” Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! Should I inform the people so that they may rejoice?” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “If you inform them, they will rely (only) on this (and stop acting).” And Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith at the time of his death, fearing the sin of concealing knowledge."
"106","Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Allah is not shy of the truth, so (please tell me), is ghusl (ritual bath) obligatory upon a woman when she has a wet dream?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “Yes, if she sees water (i.e., semen) (on her clothes or private part).” Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) then covered her face out of shyness and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Does a woman also have a wet dream?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “Yes, may your right hand be dusty (i.e., an expression of mild rebuke), then why would the child resemble her if her fluid does not come out?”"
"107","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that: ""I used to have a lot of madhi (pre-seminal fluid) discharge, so I asked Miqdad bin Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him) to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about its ruling. So he asked, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Only wudu (ablution) is obligatory for it.'"""
"108","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man stood in the mosque and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! From which place do you command us to assume Ihram?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Madinah should assume Ihram from Dhu'l-Hulaifah, the people of Sham from Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn."" Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, people think that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also said that the people of Yemen should assume Ihram from Yalamlam. And Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say that I did not hear this clearly and explicitly from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"109","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""What should a Muhrim (one in the state of Ihram for Hajj or Umrah) wear?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""He should not wear a shirt, nor a turban, nor trousers, nor a cap, nor any garment that has been touched by saffron or wars (a kind of perfume). If sandals are not available, then he may wear leather socks, but he should cut them so that they are below the ankles."""
